# Export the fitted protein model and the cryo-EM map from a ChimeraX
# session so VMD/psfgen and mdff can work with plain PDB/MRC files.
#
# EDIT before use:
#   - SESSION_FILE below
#   - the two model numbers in the `save` commands (#N) -- inspect the
#     session first (list_chimerax_instances / list_models via the
#     chimerax MCP tools, or `open` it interactively) to find which
#     model is the atomic structure and which is the volume. Don't
#     assume #1/#2 -- confirm for this session.
#   - the two output filenames (PROTEIN.pdb, MAP.mrc)
#
# Run with:
#   run_chimerax 01_export_from_session.cxc
# (see 00_env.sh)

open SESSION_FILE.cxs

# The atomic structure model may have been moved during fitting; the map
# model usually was not. Saving PDB coordinates defaults to "scene"
# coordinates, which already bakes in any fit -- see ChimeraX docs,
# "save" command, "Saving Maps after Fitting". If instead the MAP was
# moved to fit a stationary structure, swap which one gets the plain
# save vs. needs `relModel`.
save PROTEIN.pdb #2

# If this model's own grid was not moved, it's safe to write out as-is.
save MAP.mrc #1

exit
